WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:06.337
Lab 1 runs in the hr-lifecycle folder,
and nothing signs in or sends a request.

3
00:00:06.337 --> 00:00:08.900
Step one lists two tasks' reads.

4
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:11.160
The plan needs only one permission,

5
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:15.525
the Lifecycle Workflows workflow
read, for one GET on the workflows.

6
00:00:15.525 --> 00:00:19.766
Readiness needs four permissions,
for three GET calls: the users,

7
00:00:19.766 --> 00:00:24.888
each workflow's user processing results,
and the access package assignments.

8
00:00:24.888 --> 00:00:29.749
Step two lints the program's own six
workflow files with a budget of fifty.

9
00:00:29.749 --> 00:00:33.900
Zero findings, zero warnings,
zero information items.

10
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.583
That's the clean run an ISSO keeps:
it shows a one-time pass of at most

11
00:00:38.583 --> 00:00:43.680
twenty-four hours, and an execution
limit on every scheduled workflow.
